          created: 1789403481439
          modified: 1789404110801
          isPrivate: false
          description: |-
            ## Testing `createQuestionController`

            This endpoint needs **URL params**, **headers**, and a **JSON body**.

            ---

            ### 1. Route Definition

            ```javascript
            router.post("/admin/events/:eventId/questions", createQuestionController);
            ```

            ---

            ### 2. Request Breakdown

            | Part | Value |
            |------|-------|
            | **Method** | `POST` |
            | **Path** | `/admin/events/:eventId/questions` |
            | **Params** | `eventId` |
            | **Query** | ❌ None |
            | **Body** | ✅ JSON (question fields) |
            | **Headers** | `Authorization: Bearer <token>`, `Content-Type: application/json` |

            ---

            ### 3. Endpoint URL

            Using your event id: `d29c3e26-9d91-4d59-b19b-00887df452fb`

            ```
            POST http://localhost:PORT/api/admin/events/d29c3e26-9d91-4d59-b19b-00887df452fb/questions
            ```

            ---

            ### 4. Headers

            ```http
            Authorization: Bearer <your_jwt_token>
            Content-Type: application/json
            ```

            ---

            ### 5. Body — All Supported Fields

            | Field | Type | Required | Notes |
            |-------|------|----------|-------|
            | `question_text` | string | ✅ | The question itself |
            | `question_type` | enum | ✅ | `text`, `textarea`, `number`, `email`, `phone`, `date`, `time`, `datetime`, `select`, `multiselect`, `radio`, `checkbox`, `checkboxes`, `file`, `rating`, `url` |
            | `options` | array | conditional | Required for `select`, `multiselect`, `radio`, `checkboxes`. Format: `[{ label, value }]` |
            | `validation_rules` | object | ❌ | e.g. `{ min, max, minLength, maxLength, pattern }` |
            | `placeholder` | string | ❌ | Input placeholder |
            | `help_text` | string | ❌ | Helper text below input |
            | `is_required` | boolean | ❌ | Default: `false` |
            | `is_active` | boolean | ❌ | Default: `true` |
            | `display_order` | number | ❌ | Default: `0` |
            | `ask_timing` | enum | ❌ | `before_registration` (default), `after_registration`, `after_event` |
            | `conditional_logic` | object | ❌ | e.g. `{ depends_on_question_id, operator, value }` |
            | `internal_note` | string | ❌ | Admin-only note |
            | `is_admin_only` | boolean | ❌ | Default: `false` |
            | `include_in_export` | boolean | ❌ | Default: `true` |

            > ⚠️ Do **not** send `event_id`, `created_by`, `updated_by` — the controller injects them automatically from `req.params.eventId` and `req.user.sub`.

            ---

            ### 6. Postman / Thunder Client Setup

            ```
            Method: POST
            URL:    {{base_url}}/api/admin/events/d29c3e26-9d91-4d59-b19b-00887df452fb/questions

            Headers:
              Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
              Content-Type: application/json

            Body (raw JSON):
            ```

            ---

            ### 7. Example Bodies — By Question Type

            #### A. Simple Text Question

            ```json
            {
              "question_text": "What is your full name?",
              "question_type": "text",
              "is_required": true,
              "placeholder": "Enter your full name",
              "ask_timing": "before_registration",
              "display_order": 0
            }
            ```

            #### B. Select (Dropdown)

            ```json
            {
              "question_text": "What is your T-shirt size?",
              "question_type": "select",
              "options": [
                { "label": "Small", "value": "S" },
                { "label": "Medium", "value": "M" },
                { "label": "Large", "value": "L" },
                { "label": "XL", "value": "XL" }
              ],
              "is_required": true,
              "ask_timing": "before_registration",
              "display_order": 1
            }
            ```

            #### C. Checkboxes (Multiple Choice)

            ```json
            {
              "question_text": "Do you have any dietary restrictions?",
              "question_type": "checkboxes",
              "options": [
                { "label": "Vegetarian", "value": "vegetarian" },
                { "label": "Vegan", "value": "vegan" },
                { "label": "Gluten-free", "value": "gluten_free" },
                { "label": "Nut allergy", "value": "nut_allergy" }
              ],
              "is_required": false,
              "ask_timing": "before_registration",
              "display_order": 2
            }
            ```

            #### D. Rating (After Event)

            ```json
            {
              "question_text": "How would you rate the event?",
              "question_type": "rating",
              "validation_rules": { "min": 1, "max": 5 },
              "is_required": true,
              "ask_timing": "after_event",
              "display_order": 0
            }
            ```

            #### E. Number with Validation

            ```json
            {
              "question_text": "How many years of experience do you have?",
              "question_type": "number",
              "validation_rules": { "min": 0, "max": 50 },
              "placeholder": "e.g. 5",
              "is_required": false,
              "ask_timing": "before_registration",
              "display_order": 3
            }
            ```

            #### F. Email

            ```json
            {
              "question_text": "What is your email address?",
              "question_type": "email",
              "validation_rules": { "pattern": "^[^@]+@[^@]+\\.[^@]+$" },
              "is_required": true,
              "ask_timing": "before_registration",
              "display_order": 4
            }
            ```

            #### G. Admin-Only Question (hidden from attendees)

            ```json
            {
              "question_text": "Internal: Did attendee check in at the door?",
              "question_type": "checkbox",
              "is_admin_only": true,
              "is_required": false,
              "ask_timing": "after_event",
              "display_order": 5
            }
            ```

            #### H. Conditional Question (show only if another answered)

            ```json
            {
              "question_text": "Which dietary meal would you prefer?",
              "question_type": "select",
              "options": [
                { "label": "Vegan meal", "value": "vegan_meal" },
                { "label": "Vegetarian meal", "value": "veg_meal" }
              ],
              "conditional_logic": {
                "depends_on_question_id": "REPLACE_WITH_QUESTION_UUID",
                "operator": "includes",
                "value": "vegan"
              },
              "is_required": true,
              "ask_timing": "before_registration",
              "display_order": 3
            }
            ```



            > 💡 **Tip**: If you plan to create many questions for the same event at once, use the `bulkCreateQuestionsRepository` inside a service that accepts `{ eventData, questions }` — that's the `createEventWithQuestionsService` pattern we discussed earlier. This single-question endpoint is best for incremental admin edits.
          sortKey: -1751675384567
