      - url: "{{local}}/question/events/d29c3e26-9d91-4d59-b19b-00887df452fb/responses"
        name: Submit a responses
        meta:
          id: req_2bd045fcd8694f1798f7c4d3ef7bfe33
          created: 1789404242933
          modified: 1789404476302
          isPrivate: false
          description: |-
            ## Testing `submitQuestionResponsesController`

            Using the 5 questions you just created for event `d29c3e26-9d91-4d59-b19b-00887df452fb`.

            ---

            ### 1. Route Definition

            ```javascript
            router.post("/events/:eventId/questions/responses", submitQuestionResponsesController);
            ```

            ---

            ### 2. Request Breakdown

            | Part | Value |
            |------|-------|
            | **Method** | `POST` |
            | **Path** | `/events/:eventId/questions/responses` |
            | **Params** | `eventId` |
            | **Query** | ❌ None |
            | **Body** | ✅ JSON — `{ eventId, responses: [...] }` |
            | **Headers** | `Authorization: Bearer <token>`, `Content-Type: application/json` |

            > 💡 Note: your controller reads `eventId` from **`req.body`**, not from `req.params`. Both are available, but the body one is what's used.

            ---

            ### 3. Endpoint URL

            ```
            POST http://localhost:PORT/api/events/d29c3e26-9d91-4d59-b19b-00887df452fb/questions/responses
            ```

            ---

            ### 4. Body Structure

            ```json
            {
              "eventId": "<event_uuid>",
              "responses": [
                {
                  "question_id": "<question_uuid>",
                  "registration_id": "<optional_registration_uuid_or_null>",
                  "response_value": <string | number | boolean | array | object>
                }
              ]
            }
            ```

            | Field | Required | Notes |
            |-------|----------|-------|
            | `eventId` | ✅ | Must match `eventId` in URL (or just body — controller uses body) |
            | `responses[]` | ✅ | At least 1 item |
            | `responses[].question_id` | ✅ | UUID of the question |
            | `responses[].registration_id` | ❌ | Optional; null if not linked to a registration |
            | `responses[].response_value` | ✅ | Type depends on question_type |

            ---

            ### 5. Mapping Your 5 Questions → Response Values

            | # | Question | `question_id` | `question_type` | `response_value` type |
            |---|----------|---------------|-----------------|------------------------|
            | 1 | Full name | `8ccb0707-09ad-4fac-86cd-b3a380575fb8` | `text` | string |
            | 2 | T-shirt size | `e97305cb-8b8e-434a-83d2-57b618647bdd` | `select` | string (the `value`, e.g. `"M"`) |
            | 3 | Years of experience | `1b344d89-4271-4e3d-b1a5-777659d3687c` | `number` | number (0–50) |
            | 4 | Email | `65533286-eeba-46e2-a84a-873027c8f1c0` | `email` | string |
            | 5 | Dietary meal | `c83ac1da-f16c-421a-93ab-6597bee38662` | `select` | string (`"vegan_meal"` / `"veg_meal"`) |

            ---

            ### 6. Complete Example Body

            ```json
            {
              "eventId": "d29c3e26-9d91-4d59-b19b-00887df452fb",
              "responses": [
                {
                  "question_id": "8ccb0707-09ad-4fac-86cd-b3a380575fb8",
                  "response_value": "Jane Wanjiku"
                },
                {
                  "question_id": "e97305cb-8b8e-434a-83d2-57b618647bdd",
                  "response_value": "M"
                },
                {
                  "question_id": "1b344d89-4271-4e3d-b1a5-777659d3687c",
                  "response_value": 5
                },
                {
                  "question_id": "65533286-eeba-46e2-a84a-873027c8f1c0",
                  "response_value": "jane@example.com"
                },
                {
                  "question_id": "c83ac1da-f16c-421a-93ab-6597bee38662",
                  "response_value": "vegan_meal"
                }
              ]
            }
            ```


            ---

            ### 7. Response Value Types — By Question Type

            | `question_type` | Send this `response_value` |
            |-----------------|----------------------------|
            | `text` / `textarea` / `email` / `phone` / `url` | `"some string"` |
            | `number` / `rating` | `5` (a number, not `"5"`) |
            | `date` | `"2026-05-10"` (ISO date string) |
            | `time` | `"14:30"` |
            | `datetime` | `"2026-05-10T14:30:00Z"` |
            | `select` / `radio` | `"option_value"` (the `value`, not `label`) |
            | `multiselect` / `checkboxes` | `["vegan", "gluten_free"]` (array of values) |
            | `checkbox` | `true` or `false` |
            | `file` | `"https://s3.../file-url"` (uploaded URL) |

            ---

            ### 8. Expected Responses

            #### ✅ Success — `201 Created`

            ```json
            {
              "message": "Responses submitted successfully"
            }
            ```

            #### ❌ Missing fields — `422 Unprocessable Entity`

            ```json
            {
              "error": "eventId and responses array are required"
            }
            ```

            Triggered when:
            - `eventId` is missing
            - `responses` is not an array
            - `responses` is an empty array

            #### ❌ Auth failure — `401 Unauthorized`

            ```json
            {
              "error": "Access denied. No token provided."
            }
            ```

            #### ❌ Database error — `500 Internal Server Error`

            ```json
            {
              "error": "Failed to submit responses",
              "details": "insert or update on table \"question_responses\" violates foreign key constraint..."
            }
            ```

            Common causes:
            - `question_id` doesn't exist
            - `event_id` doesn't exist
            - Duplicate response (if you have a unique constraint)

            ---

            ### 9. Full Test Flow (End-to-End)

            1. **Get questions to know the IDs**:
               ```
               GET /api/events/d29c3e26-9d91-4d59-b19b-00887df452fb/questions?timing=before_registration
               ```

            2. **Submit responses** (this endpoint):
               ```
               POST /api/events/d29c3e26-9d91-4d59-b19b-00887df452fb/questions/responses
               ```

            3. **Verify responses were saved** (admin view):
               ```
               GET /api/admin/questions/e97305cb-8b8e-434a-83d2-57b618647bdd/responses
               ```

            4. **See aggregated stats** (admin dashboard):
               ```
               GET /api/admin/events/d29c3e26-9d91-4d59-b19b-00887df452fb/questions/dashboard
               ```

            ---

            ### 10. Conditional Logic Gotcha ⚠️

            Your question #5 (`Which dietary meal would you prefer?`) has:

            ```json
            "conditional_logic": {
              "value": "vegan",
              "operator": "includes",
              "depends_on_question_id": "4315674e-f65d-4609-8ce5-561fe8558d2e"
            }
            ```

            This means **your frontend** should only show that question when the answer to question `4315674e-...` includes `"vegan"`. But your **backend controller doesn't enforce this** — it will accept a response to Q5 regardless.


            ---

            ### 11. Quick Reference Table

            | What | Where | Value |
            |------|-------|-------|
            | `eventId` (URL) | Path | `d29c3e26-9d91-4d59-b19b-00887df452fb` |
            | `eventId` (body) | JSON | Same as URL |
            | Auth | Header | `Authorization: Bearer <token>` |
            | Content-Type | Header | `application/json` |
            | Body | Raw JSON | `{ eventId, responses: [...] }` |
            | Max responses | — | No limit (bulk insert) |
            | User ID | Auto | From `req.user.sub` |

            ---

            ### 12. Common Gotchas

            | Issue | Cause | Fix |
            |-------|-------|-----|
            | `422` | `responses` empty or missing | Send at least one response |
            | `500` FK violation | Invalid `question_id` | Use IDs from the questions GET |
            | `"5"` stored instead of `5` | Sent string for number type | Send raw number |
            | Duplicate row error | Unique constraint on `(question_id, user_id, event_id)` | Delete old response first or use upsert |
            | Conditional question accepted wrongly | No backend validation | Add conditional validator (see §13) |

            ---

            > 💡 **Tip**: For robustness, consider adding an **upsert** mode to `submitQuestionResponsesController` so users editing their responses don't hit unique-constraint errors. Ask me if you want that variant.
          sortKey: -1751675384542
