      - url: "{{local}}/question/admin/events/d29c3e26-9d91-4d59-b19b-00887df452fb/reor\
          der"
        name: Reorder Questions by id
        meta:
          id: req_20a5fc81686441a8aafd5f6f3227d6ca
          created: 1789405805741
          modified: 1789405918815
          isPrivate: false
          description: |-
            ## Testing `reorderQuestionsController`

            This endpoint takes **URL params**, **headers**, and a **JSON body** with the new order.

            ---

            ### 1. Route Definition

            ```javascript
            router.patch("/admin/events/:eventId/reorder", reorderQuestionsController);
            ```

            ---

            ### 2. Request Breakdown

            | Part | Value |
            |------|-------|
            | **Method** | `PATCH` |
            | **Path** | `/admin/events/:eventId/questions/reorder` |
            | **Params** | `eventId` |
            | **Query** | ❌ None |
            | **Body** | ✅ JSON — `{ order: [{ id, display_order }, ...] }` |
            | **Headers** | `Authorization: Bearer <token>`, `Content-Type: application/json` |

            ---

            ### 3. Endpoint URL

            ```
            PATCH http://localhost:PORT/api/admin/events/d29c3e26-9d91-4d59-b19b-00887df452fb/questions/reorder
            ```

            ---

            ### 4. Body Structure

            ```json
            {
              "order": [
                { "id": "<question_uuid>", "display_order": <number> },
                ...
              ]
            }
            ```

            | Field | Required | Notes |
            |-------|----------|-------|
            | `order` | ✅ | Must be a **non-empty array** |
            | `order[].id` | ✅ | UUID of the question |
            | `order[].display_order` | ✅ | New position (0-based or any number — controller just writes it) |

            > ⚠️ Do **not** send `eventId`, `updated_by`, etc. — the controller injects them from the URL and `req.user.sub`.

            ---

            ### 5. Example — Reordering Your 7 Questions

            Suppose you want to move `after_event` questions to the **front** for testing.

            Question IDs from your event:

            | Question | Current `display_order` | Current timing |
            |----------|------------------------|----------------|
            | Full name (`8ccb0707-...`) | 0 | before_registration |
            | T-shirt size (`e97305cb-...`) | 1 | before_registration |
            | Years of experience (`1b344d89-...`) | 3 | before_registration |
            | Email (`65533286-...`) | 4 | before_registration |
            | Dietary meal (`c83ac1da-...`) | 6 | before_registration |
            | Rate the event (`b3a89de4-...`) | 0 | after_event |
            | Check-in (`4315674e-...`) | 5 | after_event |

            **Reorder to: rate → check-in → full name → t-shirt → years → email → dietary:**

            ```json
            {
              "order": [
                { "id": "b3a89de4-403c-4bf1-9d69-e7b50c419e80", "display_order": 0 },
                { "id": "4315674e-f65d-4609-8ce5-561fe8558d2e", "display_order": 1 },
                { "id": "8ccb0707-09ad-4fac-86cd-b3a380575fb8", "display_order": 2 },
                { "id": "e97305cb-8b8e-434a-83d2-57b618647bdd", "display_order": 3 },
                { "id": "1b344d89-4271-4e3d-b1a5-777659d3687c", "display_order": 4 },
                { "id": "65533286-eeba-46e2-a84a-873027c8f1c0", "display_order": 5 },
                { "id": "c83ac1da-f16c-421a-93ab-6597bee38662", "display_order": 6 }
              ]
            }
            ```

            ---

            ### 6. Postman / Thunder Client Setup

            ```
            Method: PATCH
            URL:    {{base_url}}/api/admin/events/d29c3e26-9d91-4d59-b19b-00887df452fb/questions/reorder

            Headers:
              Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
              Content-Type: application/json

            Body (raw JSON):
            ```

            Paste the JSON above.

            ---

            ### 7. Sample cURL

            ```bash
            curl -X PATCH "http://localhost:3000/api/admin/events/d29c3e26-9d91-4d59-b19b-00887df452fb/questions/reorder" \
              -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN" \
              -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
              -d '{
                "order": [
                  { "id": "b3a89de4-403c-4bf1-9d69-e7b50c419e80", "display_order": 0 },
                  { "id": "4315674e-f65d-4609-8ce5-561fe8558d2e", "display_order": 1 },
                  { "id": "8ccb0707-09ad-4fac-86cd-b3a380575fb8", "display_order": 2 }
                ]
              }'
            ```

            ---

            ### 8. Axios / Frontend Example

            ```javascript
            import axios from "axios";

            const reorderQuestions = async (eventId, order) => {
              const { data } = await axios.patch(
                `${import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL}/admin/events/${eventId}/questions/reorder`,
                { order },
                {
                  headers: {
                    Authorization: `Bearer ${localStorage.getItem("token")}`,
                    "Content-Type": "application/json"
                  }
                }
              );
              return data;
            };

            // Usage — e.g. from a drag-and-drop list
            reorderQuestions("d29c3e26-9d91-4d59-b19b-00887df452fb", [
              { id: "b3a89de4-403c-4bf1-9d69-e7b50c419e80", display_order: 0 },
              { id: "4315674e-f65d-4609-8ce5-561fe8558d2e", display_order: 1 },
              { id: "8ccb0707-09ad-4fac-86cd-b3a380575fb8", display_order: 2 }
            ]);
            ```

            ---

            ### 9. Expected Responses

            #### ✅ Success — `200 OK`

            ```json
            {
              "message": "Questions reordered successfully"
            }
            ```

            #### ❌ Empty or missing `order` — `422 Unprocessable Entity`

            ```json
            {
              "error": "order array is required"
            }
            ```

            Triggered by:
            - `order` not present
            - `order` isn't an array
            - `order` is `[]`

            #### ❌ Auth failure — `401 Unauthorized`

            ```json
            {
              "error": "Access denied. No token provided."
            }
            ```

            #### ❌ DB error — `500 Internal Server Error`

            ```json
            {
              "error": "Failed to reorder questions",
              "details": "invalid input syntax for type uuid: \"not-a-uuid\""
            }
            ```

            ---

            ### 10. Verify the Reorder Worked

            After the PATCH, hit:

            ```
            GET /api/admin/events/d29c3e26-9d91-4d59-b19b-00887df452fb/questions
            ```

            The `display_order` values should reflect your new order. Note: the admin list **orders by `ask_timing` first, then `display_order`**, so questions with the same `ask_timing` will be sorted by your new `display_order` within that group.

            If you want a **global order regardless of timing**, change the repository order to:

            ```javascript
            order: [['display_order', 'ASC']]
            ```

            ---

            ### 11. Recommended Frontend Drag-and-Drop Payload

            When using a DnD library (react-beautiful-dnd, dnd-kit, etc.), send **all** questions in their new order with sequential `display_order`:

            ```javascript
            const handleDragEnd = (result) => {
              if (!result.destination) return;

              const reordered = Array.from(questions);
              const [moved] = reordered.splice(result.source.index, 1);
              reordered.splice(result.destination.index, 0, moved);

              const order = reordered.map((q, idx) => ({
                id: q.id,
                display_order: idx
              }));

              reorderQuestions(eventId, order);
            };
            ```

            ---

            ### 12. Quick Reference Table

            | What | Where | Value |
            |------|-------|-------|
            | `eventId` | URL path | `d29c3e26-9d91-4d59-b19b-00887df452fb` |
            | Auth | Header | `Authorization: Bearer <token>` |
            | Content-Type | Header | `application/json` |
            | Body | Raw JSON | `{ order: [{ id, display_order }] }` |
            | Auto-injected | DB | `updated_by` from `req.user.sub` |
            | Min items | — | 1 |

            ---

            ### 13. Common Gotchas

            | Issue | Cause | Fix |
            |-------|-------|-----|
            | `422` | Sent `order: []` | Send at least 1 item |
            | `422` | Sent `order` as object | Must be an array |
            | `500` | Invalid UUID in `order[].id` | Use real question IDs |
            | Partial update silently succeeds | One ID doesn't belong to the event | The repo filters by `event_id` so unknown IDs are just no-ops |
            | Wrong order after reload | Reading grouped by `ask_timing` | Change repo order to `['display_order', 'ASC']` if you want global order |

            ---

            > 💡 **Tip**: If you want **strict validation** (e.g. reject any `id` not in the event, or reject duplicate IDs), add a pre-check in the service:
            > ```javascript
            > const existing = await DynamicQuestion.findAll({ where: { event_id: eventId }, attributes: ['id'] });
            > const validIds = new Set(existing.map(q => q.id));
            > const invalid = order.filter(o => !validIds.has(o.id));
            > if (invalid.length) throw new Error(`Unknown question IDs: ${invalid.map(o => o.id).join(', ')}`);
            > ```
            > Say the word if you want me to add that.
          sortKey: -1751675384529.5
        method: PATCH
        body:
          mimeType: application/json
          text: >-
            {
              "order": [
                { "id": "b3a89de4-403c-4bf1-9d69-e7b50c419e80", "display_order": 0 },
                { "id": "4315674e-f65d-4609-8ce5-561fe8558d2e", "display_order": 1 },
                { "id": "8ccb0707-09ad-4fac-86cd-b3a380575fb8", "display_order": 2 },
                { "id": "e97305cb-8b8e-434a-83d2-57b618647bdd", "display_order": 3 },
                { "id": "1b344d89-4271-4e3d-b1a5-777659d3687c", "display_order": 4 },
